      "message": "When the client opens a stream, it may use the minimum buffer size suggested by the HAL within the returned `AudioPatch`, see here: https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:hardware/interfaces/audio/aidl/default/Module.cpp;l\u003d1126;drc\u003dbe5b10f9022f6e4aeab9c39f50c1e6ac27e19eae.\n\nAs I understand it, for non-PCM cases that value can also end up being too large. So I think we need to address the minimum buffer size calculation in `Module::setAudioPatch` as well.\n\nIt might also make sense to rename `calculateBufferSizeFrames` to `calculateBufferSizeFramesForPcm` to emphasize the fact that it should not be used for non-PCM streams.",
